    "customfield_12313320": "<div style='font-weight:bold;color:red;text-align:center'>This project has a <a href=\"https://lucene.apache.org/core/discussion.html\">user mailing list and an IRC channel</a> for support. If you are looking for support, or if you are not sure whether the behavior that you are observing is expected or not, please discuss it there first.</div>",
    "customfield_12314134": null,
    "duedate": null,
    "customfield_12314132": null,
    "customfield_12314131": null,
    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12426142/comment/12712269",
          "id": "12712269",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=earwin",
            "name": "earwin",
            "key": "earwin",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Earwin Burrfoot",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "Let's have string key-value pairs per-segment, per-commit, per-index?\nLucene can store debugging data there, user can add something if he needs.\n\nWe can design some unified metadata interface available through IndexReader and won't expose SegmentInfo (doing this with our current back-compat policies is akin to suicide)",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=earwin",
            "name": "earwin",
            "key": "earwin",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Earwin Burrfoot",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2009-05-22T21:24:16.660+0000",
          "updated": "2009-05-22T21:26:58.382+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12426142/comment/12712412",
          "id": "12712412",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "bq. Let's have string key-value pairs per-segment, per-commit, per-index?\n\nThis would be great, but it's quite a bit more work than having IW include its own diagnostics per-segment.\n\nCan you open a separate issue for that?",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2009-05-23T11:47:59.784+0000",
          "updated": "2009-05-23T11:47:59.784+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12426142/comment/12712413",
          "id": "12712413",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=earwin",
            "name": "earwin",
            "key": "earwin",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Earwin Burrfoot",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "We can start with string key-value pairs per-segment that are created only from inside Lucene and leave everything else for the latter.\n\nWhat I'm trying to avoid is writing a partial solution, then a more generic one (with different implementation) and having to keep that partial solution around because it was already released. I.e. you're going to extend segment file format, right? Let it be key-value pairs from the start, instead of a single Int that is predetermined to be Lucene's version.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=earwin",
            "name": "earwin",
            "key": "earwin",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Earwin Burrfoot",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2009-05-23T12:03:07.520+0000",
          "updated": "2009-05-23T12:03:07.520+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12426142/comment/12712424",
          "id": "12712424",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "OK I'll start with that.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
